{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/933988-how-often-do-you-use-solar-npcs","id":933988,"title":"How often do you use Solar NPCs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-19T11:22:36-07:00","id":933988,"title":"How often do you use Solar NPCs?","content":"I am rather curious how often Solars show up as NPCs in most games and how they are portrayed? I mostly mean fairly notable characters not so much a Wyld Hunt boss.<br /> <br /> A secondary question is whether you use existing NPC Exalts in your games or rely entirely on custom NPCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 07-19-2016, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:13:34-07:00","id":934011,"title":"","content":"1) Solar's occasionally show up in the games I run. While Solar's are very rare in Creation, they tend to either get caught up in, or are drawn to major events in Creation. So as long as the group of players are involved in big events, it's inevitable that they'll meet the occasional Solar.<br /> <br /> 2) I use established NPCs like: Lytek, Chejop Kejak, Peleps Deled, etc. if that's what you mean. If you're asking if I use NPCs like Dace, Swan, or Arianna, then the answers &quot;no&quot;. I think there's a distinction between setting NPCs (ie. gods, Deathlords, significant Realm players, etc), and the canon Exalts for each splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:23:03-07:00","id":934015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/933988-how-often-do-you-use-solar-npcs?p=934011#post934011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)<br /> 2) I use established NPCs like: Lytek, Chejop Kejak, Peleps Deled, etc. if that's what you mean. If you're asking if I use NPCs like Dace, Swan, or Arianna, then the answers &quot;no&quot;. I think there's a distinction between setting NPCs (ie. gods, Deathlords, significant Realm players, etc), and the canon Exalts for each splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya, I should have been more clear on that. I was mostly referring to NPC Exalts beyond the major players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:51:01-07:00","id":934027,"title":"","content":"To the first: maybe if I need an antagonist for Dynastic PCs, or if I'm running a solo game.<br /> <br /> To the second: no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:55:09-07:00","id":934037,"title":"","content":"Signature Characters like Nova, Swan, and the like are meant to be example PC characters. I don't use them in games.<br /> <br /> Now, Solars like the Bull of the North? I would use him in a game. Mostly as an antagonist. Maybe as an adviser if the Solar PCs are passing though the North. If the Solar PCs are based in the North, I'd leave him out. I rather have one of the PCs unite the Ice Walker tribes than a NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T06:02:33-07:00","id":934432,"title":"","content":"In the last campaign I ran, our characters never met other Solars (they did meet pretty much every other type of Exalt, from Lunars to Infernal, Sids and Dragon-Blooded). In my current campaign, while they haven't met other Solars (and really, haven't met a lot of other Exalts either right now : a grand total of two in the first 8 sessions), they have heard rumors and stories about the anathema Visadhara, the Fosaken also refered to as the Bane of Ansibah, apparently operating in the same region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T06:26:23-07:00","id":934446,"title":"","content":"Mostly what I get the most out of:<br /> -Solars in the cult of Illuminated, mostly to show Solars like them who are working with the cult.<br /> -Sometime you have Solars saviors, like the heroes come to save a region but a Solar already on it.<br /> -Children and people exalting in some situations, having the party to offer more help and guidance to a fresh new Solar.<br /> -Occasional Solars having the opposed motivations/ideas as the circle.<br /> <br /> As for existing npcs, it depends sometime but mostly as Cameos. Emissary no big spoilers involved in my games is a first age solar.<br /> <br /> edit: Special bonus story: Solars come to save a village and guide the fools into a better age. Twist: The Solars are indeed coming...you aren't the solars, Players are Mortals in the village (prelude story to exaltation.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2127,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","user":"Eltacolibre","date":". 07-20-2016, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T06:55:33-07:00","id":934463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/933988-how-often-do-you-use-solar-npcs#post933988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am rather curious how often Solars show up as NPCs in most games and how they are portrayed? I mostly mean fairly notable characters not so much a Wyld Hunt boss.<br /> <br /> A secondary question is whether you use existing NPC Exalts in your games or rely entirely on custom NPCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Rarely, but it does happen. My current game, though, is set before Game Start, so the closest thing they have encountered are First Age Ghosts of &quot;Solar Anathema.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. I use canon NPCs, including the example ones, as well as my own. My games tend to have a large cast of characters, and the canon NPCs are too handy for shared world building to pass up. All my players know Tepet Arada, so getting the desired reaction is easier with him than somebody I just make up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T07:30:03-07:00","id":934482,"title":"","content":"So in the chronicle I'm currently running, I have a NPC full solar circle that operate in the Western Oceans. Their Eclipse, striving to bring her father's dream to fruition, is working to unify the plethora of pirate crews into a federation. This circle is a bit of a special snowflake as it's the PC circle from my first exalted game I ran in 1st ed. Two of my current players were in that game so it's a bit of a nostalgia bomb. I have used them to give my current circle a chance to see how a different circle works and a sense that, while they are rare, they aren't alone. I do have other plans for them as well ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T08:16:42-07:00","id":934501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/933988-how-often-do-you-use-solar-npcs?p=934432#post934432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the last campaign I ran, our characters never met other Solars (they did meet pretty much every other type of Exalt, from Lunars to Infernal, Sids and Dragon-Blooded). In my current campaign, while they haven't met other Solars (and really, haven't met a lot of other Exalts either right now : a grand total of two in the first 8 sessions), they have heard rumors and stories about the anathema Visadhara, the Fosaken also refered to as the Bane of Ansibah, apparently operating in the same region.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any word on Ebele?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T11:58:08-07:00","id":934631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/933988-how-often-do-you-use-solar-npcs?p=934501#post934501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any word on Ebele?</div> </div> </div> </div>^^ Hey, someone who read Poisoned Shores! Ebele is somewhat of a recurring character, being the cousin of our Eclipse. She's busy fighting pirates at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:32:26-07:00","id":934648,"title":"","content":"I used them a bit in my 2nd ed game, as people for some of the PCs who joined the Cult of the Illuminated to meet.<br /> But, honestly, I found that they were all pretty bland, so they all ended up getting turned into Abyssals and fighting the PCs for their master, Walker in Darkness.<br /> <br /> This time, I've used Solar NPCs again, but in a different way. This time, they're the villains (or anti-heroes?) that the PCs are matching up against. There's a circle of Essence 3 Solars (the PCs are Essence 5), for them to fight (well, or ally with, but since they stabbed the NPC Eclipse I guess that's not happening).<br /> I wouldn't want to have random Solar NPCs cross path with the PCs like in the old game though: I think every Solar they meet ought to be somewhat significant.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have used canon NPCs, especially early in the game, since I thought it'd make them more significant to the players than ones I made myself. But, now I'm more confidant of my NPCs, and I only use ones that matter because they were in the previous game (for example, Ledaal Kes, who fought them before, is now Satrap of the nearby Realm satrapy). I found most of the minor NPCs just weren't that interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}